.TH WEACT-CLI 1 "October 2026" "WeAct35 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
weact-cli, WeActCLI \- display text, images and codes on verified WeAct USB displays
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B weact-cli
.BI /p: PATH_OR_N
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ text ... ]
.br
.B weact-cli
.BI /p: PATH_OR_N
.B /init
.br
.B weact-cli
.BI /p: PATH_OR_N
.BI /qr: DATA
.RI [ /x:X /y:Y /w:W /h:H ]
.br
.B weact-cli
.BI /p: PATH_OR_N
.BI /barcode: FORMAT:DATA
.RI [ /x:X /y:Y /w:W /h:H ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
WeActCLI is the compatibility name for this program.  It writes only after
identifying the selected USB CDC ACM display.  FS35 is Product
.B Display FS V1
(480 by 320, RGB565 little-endian); FS096 is Product
.B Display FS 0.96 Inch
(160 by 80, legacy BRG565/MSB).  Both use VID:PID 1a86:fe0c, so Product is
also checked.  Prefer a stable path under /dev/serial/by-id.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B /p:N
Select /dev/ttyACMN, where N is 0 through 999999.
.TP
.B /p:/dev/...
Select an absolute device or by-id path.  A port is required for an operation.
.TP
.B --serial SERIAL
Require the matching USB serial.
.TP
.B /v
Write model/canvas diagnostics to standard error.
.TP
.B --allow-unknown-occupancy
Accept only the limited foreign-process permission case after identity checks.
It does not bypass a known busy port, an identity failure, or a scanner/
namespace failure.
.TP
.B /?, /h, --help
Show usage without device access.
.SH TEXT AND IMAGE
Text is UTF-8 from, in priority order, /CLS, image, file, literal arguments,
or redirected stdin.  Literal arguments are joined by spaces.
.TP
.B /c:COLOR
Text colour: red, green, blue, white, black, yellow, cyan, or magenta.
.TP
.B /f:FONT[:SIZE]
Fontconfig request; size is 6 through 32, with DejaVu Sans fallback.
.TP
.B /center
Centre text or code.
.TP
.B /x:X /y:Y
For text, either coordinate enables sparse solid-glyph overlay.  It preserves
other pixels and cannot be combined with image or scrolling.
.TP
.B /CLS
Send a black clear frame.
.TP
.B /file:PATH
Read bounded UTF-8 regular-file input.
.TP
.B /image:PATH[:MODE[:WxH]]
Use PNG, JPEG, BMP, or first GIF frame.  Mode 0 fits, 1 is top-left, and 2 is
centred.  /quality accepts fast, normal, high, bw, bwfast, bwhigh, 0, 1, or 2.
.TP
.B /s:SPEED[:u|d]
One scrolling pass at pixels per second; it then clears.  Direction defaults
up.  --scroll-stats reports host measurements.  --scroll-compression off|fastlz
is explicit FS35 scrolling-only compression and defaults to off.
.SH INITIALISATION AND CODES
.B /init
is standalone and FS35-only.  It sets orientation 02, validates it, and clears
the entire screen black.  It does not reset or change brightness.  Use it after
FS35 power-on, but not between regional updates.
.PP
.B /qr:DATA
uses strict UTF-8, ECI 26 and ECC M.  A barcode is
.B /barcode:code128|ean8|ean13|code39:DATA .
Code 128 is ASCII; Code 39 uses its basic uppercase alphabet without *; EAN-8
accepts 7/8 digits and EAN-13 12/13 digits with checksum computation/validation.
Code mode is exclusive with text, images, clear, colour, font, quality and
scrolling.  It uses black modules on white, integer scaling and quiet zones;
no-fit is rejected rather than clipped.
.PP
For FS35, add all four /x:X /y:Y /w:W /h:H values to render a code in one
rectangle.  The rectangle must fit 480 by 320 including quiet zones; only that
rectangle is transmitted and unknown pixels outside it are not read.  FS096
codes are fullscreen only; regional parameters are rejected before opening it.
Fullscreen FS096 code requests landscape before its bitmap; a true overlay preserves device state.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
weact-list --verbose
weact-cli /p:/dev/serial/by-id/usb-WeAct_Studio_Display_FS_V1_YOUR_ID-if00 /init
weact-cli /p:/dev/serial/by-id/usb-WeAct_Studio_Display_FS_V1_YOUR_ID-if00 \
  '/barcode:code128:ABC123' /x:220 /y:80 /w:240 /h:100
weact-cli /p:/dev/serial/by-id/usb-WeAct_Studio_Display_FS_V1_YOUR_ID-if00 \
  '/qr:https://example.com' /x:40 /y:40 /w:160 /h:160
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 is success/help; 1 is input, rendering, identification, connection,
transport or cleanup failure; 2 is invalid arguments; 128 plus a signal is an
interrupted hardware operation.  Read stderr for guard and transport detail.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Do not retry a partial transfer or run this program and weactterm on one port
at the same time.  A guarded connection failure has no fallback port scan.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR weact-list (1),
.BR weactterm (1),
.BR libweact (3)
